type
  {
    the aiData.cfg input record :: LAYOUT OWNED BY THE TRUTH SOURCE
    <Calibration\LanU.pas:198 AiParam>. match it exactly — that project
    writes the file we read.

    Descriptor is 34 bytes, NOT 30 + CalHigh + CalLow. LanU's own note
    above the declaration explains why ::
      "CalHigh & CalLow ... 'Only used in calibration. No particular need
       to store'! (CalHigh & CalLow) shall be replaced by 4 more AnsiChar
       bytes! by expanding Descriptor by 4 bytes to accomodate for
       steinhart's d-term!"
    the retired 30+2+2 shape survives there as an <As-Found::> comment, and
    it is what this record used to declare. the byte COUNT was identical
    <77 either way>, so nothing crashed — but our CalHigh|CalLow overlaid
    descriptor bytes 31..34, read as zero, and were written back over the
    text on every save.

    the endpoints are NOT homeless :: TAuxCalibrationData already carries
    CalHigh|CalLow <MacUniModCalUtilsU>, ComputeAuxSlopeAndOffset fills
    them, and ReportsU streams them to AuxiliaryRecords.dat. that record is
    what the aux download reads them from — legacy needed a separate
    AiBoardCalHiLo array only because it had no such record.
  }
